---
description: Rename types/files when their responsibility broadens beyond the old name
alwaysApply: true
---

# Rename When Scope Changes

When you broaden a type, method, or file beyond what its name describes, rename it (and update all call sites / the `.meta` via file move) in the same change.

- Prefer a name that matches current responsibility, not the original use case.
- Example: a level-up-only billboard reused for gold/food pickups should become something like `FloatingWorldText`, not stay `NpcLevelUpFloatingText`.
- Do not leave misleading names as follow-up work unless the user explicitly asks to defer the rename.
- Always rename files with `git mv` (not delete + recreate) so Git tracks the rename; move the `.meta` the same way.
